  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The area (in sq. units) of the region bounded by the curve $x^{2}=4 y$ and the straight line $x=4 y-2$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zQzrp",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oRhU9",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VhnR4",
      "text": "$\\frac{7}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VAS1K",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/rlMJ6CC3lOq6tClVsG7jaXtCd1AA0ppl6i_tFAiV3rY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nLet points of intersection of the curve and the line be\r\n\r\n$P$ and $Q$\r\n\r\n$x^{2}=4\\left(\\frac{x+2}{4}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$x^{2}-x-2=0$\r\n\r\n$x=2,-1$\r\n\r\nPoint are (2,1) and $\\left(-1, \\frac{1}{4}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\text { Area }=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left[\\left(\\frac{x+2}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{4}\\right)\\right] d x=\\left[\\frac{x^{2}}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} x-\\frac{x^{3}}{12}\\right]_{-1}^{2}$\r\n\r\n$=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+1-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{12}\\right)=\\frac{9}{8}$",
    "image": null
  },
